# IDauto migration manifest — THE order in which the database is built.
#
# Single source of truth (IDA-G9, 2026-11-25). Read by scripts/migrate.js
# (`npm run migrate`) and, through it, by .github/workflows/database.yml.
# tests/ida-migration-manifest-test.js fails when a file in this directory is
# missing from this list, listed twice, or listed but absent on disk.
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#
#   <path relative to database/>   <probe>[, <probe> ...]
#
# A probe is a read-only catalogue check that is true once the file has been
# applied. They let `npm run migrate -- --baseline` adopt a database that was
# migrated by hand (docs/DATABASE.md §1a) without running anything again:
#
#   table <name>                 the table exists
#   column <table>.<column>      the column exists
#   index <name>                 the index exists
#   constraint <name>            the constraint exists
#   constraint <name> has <txt>  ... and its definition contains <txt>
#   nullable <table>.<column>    the column exists and accepts NULL
#
# Probe what the file creates LAST (or the change only it makes), so that a
# partially applied file is not mistaken for an applied one.
#
# Adding a migration: append ONE line at the end, with a probe. Never edit or
# reorder a line that a database has already applied — the runner records a
# sha256 of every applied file and refuses to run when one changed.
#
# DEPLOY-ORDER HAZARD (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §9): migrations/ida-v13b-auth-account-issuer.sql
# must be applied BEFORE the code that ships Better Auth >= 1.7.3 is started.
# Running `npm run migrate` before the restart satisfies that; the runner never
# restarts anything.
#
# database/seed-synthetic-test-data.sql is NOT a migration and is not listed:
# it is synthetic test data for scratch databases only.

